course: dictionary
lesson: 14905
title: When something comes back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A recurrence is when something happens again. Think of a cold that returns a month after you got better: that is a recurrence of the cold. «The doctor hoped there would be no recurrence of the illness.» The doctor hoped the sick feeling would not come back.
explain: Recurrence is a noun, so it names a thing. Its clues are in the words around it. Phrases like «a recurrence of» and «to prevent a recurrence» tell you that something has come back, or might come back.
explain: In maths, recurrence has a special meaning: a rule where each number in a pattern is found from the numbers before it. In 2, 4, 8, 16, each number comes from the one before it. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Recurrence means when something happens again.
fact: «To prevent a recurrence» means to stop something happening again.
fact: «A recurrence of the illness» means the illness has come back.
fact: In maths, a recurrence is a rule where each number is found from the numbers before it.
fact: Recurrence is a noun, so you can have one recurrence or many recurrences.
exercise: «The doctor hoped there would be no recurrence of the illness.» What does recurrence mean here? | The illness going away quickly | A new doctor arriving | A sudden loud noise | *The illness coming back
exercise: «Fit a lock on the gate to prevent a recurrence of the flood.» What does prevent a recurrence mean? | Make it happen faster | Wait until the summer | Find a flood in a book | *Stop it happening again
exercise: In the pattern 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, each number is found from the ones before it. What is this rule called? | *A recurrence rule | A rhyme | A happy ending | A safety notice
test: «There was a recurrence of the cough every winter.» What does recurrence mean? | Something was lost for ever | A sudden quiet | Something brand new | *Something came back again
test: Which phrase is a clue that recurrence means something has come back? | *A risk of recurrence | Ten red cars | Sunny and bright | Blue and green
exam: In the pattern 2, 4, 8, 16, each number follows a recurrence rule. Which number comes next? | 24 | 18 | 20 | *32
